WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.220
Game of Thrones Season 7 Episode 3 begins
with Jon Snow landing on Dragonstone.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:11.080
He’s met by Tyrion, who he hasn’t seen
since Season 1 – and Jon notes that they’ve

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.259
both picked up some scars.

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:17.350
Tyrion was wounded at the Blackwater, and
Jon was attacked by an eagle.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:22.820
They’ve both suffered less visible wounds
as well – Tyrion’s betrayal by Shae, Jon’s

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.430
loss of Ygritte, and his death.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.220
Jon and Tyrion are a bastard and a dwarf,
both looked down on by society.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.990
They’ve suffered, but survived, and have
both risen high – and their bond helps make

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:37.160
this meeting possible.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.410
Davos and Missandei are here, and he mentions
her homeland of Naath.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:46.320
The Naathi are a peaceful people who worship
butterflies , but they’re preyed on by slavers

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.640
– Missandei was stolen from home as a child.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:54.149
In the books, Daenerys offers to take Missandei
back to Naath , but she prefers to stay with

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:55.430
Daenerys.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:01:00.800
Davos says Dragonstone has changed, and it’s
true –last time he was here, Davos served

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.879
Stannis, and Melisandre was burning men alive
on the beach.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:09.299
Now Dany is in charge, and Mel’s staying
outta the spotlight.

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:12.979
She watches from a cliff, and talks with Varys.

00:01:12.979 --> 00:01:17.570
Mel says that now that she got Jon and Dany
together, her job’s done, and she’s leaving

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.240
for Volantis.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.049
Maybe there she’ll meet up with other red
priests, who could help in the war for the

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.049
dawn.

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:28.189
Mel will return to Westeros, though, because
she believes that she’ll die there.

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:32.430
We also know that Mel believes that she’ll
meet Arya again.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.819
Could the two be connected?

00:01:33.819 --> 00:01:36.189
Maybe Arya will kill Melisandre.

00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:40.920
It’s also possible Mel will play the role
of Nissa Nissa – that she’ll be killed

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.520
by the hero Azor Ahai to set his sword afire.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.969
This might be Jon, with Longclaw.

00:01:46.969 --> 00:01:51.759
Mel also says that Varys will die in Westeros,
but it’s unclear how that’ll go down.

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:56.329
Maybe he’ll betray Dany and get roasted
by a dragon like she promised.

00:01:56.329 --> 00:02:01.389
We then get one of the most anticipated moments
in Thrones – the meeting of Jon Snow and

00:02:01.389 --> 00:02:03.139
Daenerys Targaryen.

00:02:03.139 --> 00:02:07.039
These two have been the protagonists of the
story since Book 1, but they’ve been a world

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:09.240
apart the entire time.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.280
Now ice and fire finally meet.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.930
And they don’t get along.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:18.500
Dany wants Jon to submit to her, because his
ancestor Torrhen Stark swore the north to

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.040
House Targaryen three hundred years ago.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.299
Jon points out that the last Targaryen king
was Dany’s father Mad Aerys, who the realm

00:02:25.299 --> 00:02:27.310
fought a war to get rid of.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.540
Dany argues it’s not her fault her dad was
crazy, and Jon says it’s not his fault his

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.030
ancestor made an oath.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:37.630
What they should really worry about, Jon says,
is the army of zombies and white walkers marching

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.069
on the seven kingdoms.

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:42.739
Dany doesn’t know nothing about the army
of zombies and walkers, all she cares about

00:02:42.739 --> 00:02:44.610
is winning her throne.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:48.110
And so Dany and Jon agree to disagree for
now.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:52.599
Dany learns that Euron destroyed her fleet,
and we briefly see Theon criticised by his

00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:54.689
men for surviving.

00:02:54.689 --> 00:02:58.530
This story just keeps finding fresh new ways
to make Theon suffer.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:04.540
At the capital, Euron rides in with his captives
– his niece Yara, and Ellaria and Tyene

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.540
Sand.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.349
It’s a little weird that the common folk
love Euron so much.

00:03:08.349 --> 00:03:14.280
The ironborn, and Euron in particular, have
a bad reputation as raiders and pirates . But,

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.830
as Euron suggests, the commons don’t really
care who’s who so long as they get a show,

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.650
and a show Euron gives.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:26.410
He’s theatrical and crude and cruel, playing
the crowd, blowing kisses, and calling people

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.410
twats.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:30.459
He rides up to Cersei and gifts her Tyene
and Ellaria.

00:03:30.459 --> 00:03:32.870
In return, Euron wants to marry Cersei.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:37.390
And Cersei says he’ll get his heart’s
desire after the war.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:41.849
The vague term heart’s desire might give
Cersei room to back out of this later.

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:45.269
In the books, by the way, it’s Daenerys
that Euron wants to marry.

00:03:45.269 --> 00:03:50.609
“When the kraken weds the dragon”, he
says, “let all the world beware” . But

00:03:50.609 --> 00:03:55.120
in the show, the Greyjoys and the Lannisters
make alliance – Euron will lead the navy,

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.629
while Jaime leads the army.

00:03:56.629 --> 00:04:01.299
There’s a rivalry between these two, which
could maybe undermine Jaime and Cersei’s

00:04:01.299 --> 00:04:02.299
relationship.

00:04:02.299 --> 00:04:07.030
In the books, Jaime eventually rejects Cersei
partly because she cheats on him . Maybe Cersei

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:10.230
will get close to Euron, and that’ll make
Jaime snap.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:15.079
In the dungeons, Cersei confronts Ellaria,
the woman who murdered her daughter Myrcella.

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:19.750
In revenge, Cersei poisons Ellaria’s daughter
Tyene, and makes Ellaria watch her daughter

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.500
die and rot to dust.

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:27.860
In the books, Ellaria is a voice for peace
, but in the show, she’s another perpetrator,

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:33.430
and now a victim of the bloody chain of vengeance
that killed Oberyn and Elia and Myrcella before

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:34.660
her.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:38.430
After murdering the Snakes, Cersei’s in
the mood for twincest, so she goes has sex

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.500
with brother Jaime.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.340
There’s a bit in the books where during
sex, Cersei says “I want”, and Jaime thinks

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.780
she means she wants him.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:51.230
But later he realises Cersei actually meant
she wanted Arya Stark dead – cause Arya’s

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.670
wolf had just hurt Joffrey.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.800
The situation’s similar here.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:58.440
Cersei throws herself at Jaime, and he probably
thinks it’s cause she loves him.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:03.030
But Cersei’s passion right now may have
more to do with the Sand Snakes she’s torturing.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:07.680
Maybe, as in the books, show-Jaime will realise
that Cersei doesn’t love him so much as

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.340
she loves herself and loves hurting others.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:15.070
The next morning, Cersei lets a maid see Jaime
in her bed, so she’s no longer trying to

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.890
hide her incestuous relationship.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:22.640
Cersei and Jaime have long dreamed of loving
each other openly , but in Westeros, incest’s

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:27.290
seen as an abomination , so this is probably
a bad PR move.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:31.110
Cersei then gets a visit from Tycho Nestoris
of the Iron Bank.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:35.630
Cersei’s regime is in lots of debt, and
the Bank wants its money back.

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:40.430
If Cersei won’t pay, Tycho threatens to
fund Daenerys instead – figuring she may

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:41.930
be a better investment.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:46.750
But Cersei argues Dany’s unreliable, and
that Dany’s anti-slavery stance is bad for

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:50.460
the Iron Bank’s profits – Tycho seems
to agree.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:51.530
Which is interesting.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:58.380
Cause the Iron Bank is based in Braavos, and
Braavos was founded by ex-slaves as an anti-slavery

00:05:58.380 --> 00:05:59.380
city.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:04.470
Its rulers oppose “slavery in all its forms”
. So would the Iron Bank of Braavos invest

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:06.060
in the slave trade?

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:10.720
Maybe they’re doing it secretly – the
Bank is famously shadowy . In fact there are

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:15.220
rumours of a connection between the Bank and
the Faceless Men , the assassins who Arya

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.190
trained with who are also based in Braavos.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.980
So there’s all sorts of possibilities going
on in the books.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.410
In the show, though, the Bank’s role is
to bankroll Cersei.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:29.530
She tells Tycho that Lannisters pay their
debts, and the Iron Bank will get its due.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:34.390
At Dragonstone, Jon complains to Tyrion that
no one believes him about the white walkers.

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:38.800
It’s a common thing in sci-fi and fantasy
for a hero to have to convince people of a

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:43.590
supernatural threat – the Reapers are coming,
Skynet will happen, the Demogorgon, Voldemort.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:48.360
It’s funny in Thrones, though, that people
are sceptical of white walkers while literal

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:50.380
dragons circle above.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.580
Dany’s storyline is full of magic.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:57.770
She’s survived fires, hatched dragons, fought
warlocks and witches, had prophetic visions.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:01.440
Is it so hard for her to believe in some frosty
zombies?

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:06.070
Maybe, as Tyrion hints, she doesn’t want
to believe, because she’s so focussed on

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:07.320
her Throne.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:11.440
So for now, Dany won’t go north, but she
does want Jon on side.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:16.200
So Tyrion suggests she give him Dragonstone’s
dragonglass – the stuff that kills white

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.340
walkers.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:22.040
Dany also brings up a comment Davos made about
Jon’s resurrection, which Tyrion dismisses

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.110
as fancy.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:28.080
Jon’s death and resurrection was probably
the biggest plot point in Thrones Seasons

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:33.920
5 and 6, if not in the whole series, yet it’s
had almost no impact on the story.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:38.520
People barely ever talk about the fact that
Jon rose from the dead, he’s Game of Thrones

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.880
Jesus, but he’s mostly unchanged.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.490
So what was the point of the resurrection?

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:48.360
Characters in the books who get resurrected
change dramatically – the same will probably

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.660
be true of book-Jon.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:53.990
Jon and Dany speak alone for the first time
ever.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:57.940
Dany mentions that one of her dragons is named
for her dead brother Rhaegar.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:02.810
And Rhaegar just happens to be Jon Snow’s
father, though he doesn’t know it yet.

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:07.640
Dany says we enjoy what we’re good at, and
Jon says he doesn’t, which again connects

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:08.640
to Rhaegar.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:13.170
Cause in Season 5, Barristan tells Dany that
while Rhaegar was great at fighting, he didn’t

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:18.660
enjoy it . Jon is also good at fighting, but
he apparently doesn’t like it either – like

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.450
father, like son.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:24.880
The connections between Jon and Rhaegar are
hinted at over and over this episode – like

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:29.720
when Jon says that he’s not a Stark, just
before a dragon swoops above – because Jon

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:32.800
is truly a Targaryen, Daenerys’ nephew.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:36.400
So – they’d better not fall in love or
anything, eh?

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:39.979
Up at Winterfell, Sansa prepares the north
for the war to come.

00:08:39.979 --> 00:08:44.860
Maester Wolkan mentions that Luwin kept copies
of every raven message – and Littlefinger

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:45.860
looks worried.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:50.330
He’s probably thinking of the message he
got Lysa to send to Catelyn saying the Lannisters

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:54.360
killed Jon Arryn – which was a lie designed
to cause conflict.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:59.300
If Wolkan or Sansa find this letter – they’d
have proof of Petyr’s betrayal.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:03.340
That particular letter was given to Catelyn
sealed, then was burned, so there may not

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:07.900
be a copy of it, but there’s still lots
of other dirt on Petyr to uncover – like

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:11.890
the fact that he lied about this dagger, and
betrayed Ned.

00:09:11.890 --> 00:09:17.280
Littlefinger has built a Jenga tower of lies
and if the Starks can grasp one piece, it

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:19.430
will all come tumbling down.

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:24.170
Petyr gives a weird speech about thinking
strategically about everyone everywhere always

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:28.860
, which might sound impressive if he was a
man with an actual plan right now.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:33.580
The fact that Yohn Royce has become a prominent
character all of a sudden may hint that Littlefinger

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:37.780
will soon be replaced as representative of
the Vale.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.650
And then Bran turns up.

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:44.280
Sansa and Bran haven’t seen each other since
Episode 1, when they were both children.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:49.860
Now, Sansa’s a political leader, and Bran
is– kind of a tree god?

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:54.450
Last season, the three-eyed raven died and
gave Bran all his power, the magic of the

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:58.970
old gods – which is a sort of a hive mind
of all of the dead greenseers and children

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:04.560
of forest and wargs connected in a network
of weirwood trees – containing this knowledge

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.580
of the past and future.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:11.590
Bran now sees everything everywhere – kind
of like what Littlefinger claimed before,

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.280
but Bran has it for real.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:17.180
He sees everything, and it’s messing with
his head.

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:22.950
Bran acts all distant and robotic with Sansa,
and insensitively brings up her marriage to

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:23.950
Ramsay.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:27.840
The reason why he’s acting weird is that
he’s just had all spacetime downloaded into

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:30.810
his skull, and he’s struggling to handle
that.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:35.210
In the words of the actor, “Bran is existing
in thousands of planes of existence at any

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:36.210
one time.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:40.300
So it’s quite difficult for Bran to have
… personality” . Not to mention, Bran

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:45.300
spent his adolescence in a tree with a wizard,
so between that and the Internet in his head,

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:47.690
it’s no surprise that he comes off as awkward.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:49.640
But he needs to sort this shit out fast.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:56.100
He needs to learn to use his power, so he’s
ready to face the walkers and the Long Night.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:11:01.860
At Oldtown, Sam’s treatment has successfully
cured Jorah of greyscale, and Jorah now has

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:03.550
a future again.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:07.740
Which is nice and all, but it takes away a
layer from his character.

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:11.820
In the books, there’s this guy called Jon
Connington who gets greyscale, and the knowledge

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:17.210
that he’s gonna die makes him really purposeful
and focussed on his goals . With greyscale,

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:22.240
he’s got nothing to lose, which makes him
a dangerous and tragic figure.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:26.810
Jorah could’ve been the same, but now that
he’s cured, he’s just back to square one.

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:29.990
At least he’s finally got a new shirt.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:34.400
In the books, Jorah’s father Jeor speaks
his last words to Sam, and says to tell Jorah

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:38.750
that he forgives him his crimes, and wants
him to join the Night’s Watch . Maybe Jorah

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:43.870
will take the black at some point in the show,
but for now Jorah’s plan is to return to

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.040
his dear Khaleesi.

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:48.970
Sam gets dragged to the headmasters office
and gets a firm talking to from Dumbledore.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:53.150
He’s pretty mad that Harry broke all the
rules, but he did save the day, so Dumbledore

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:54.750
lets him off the hook.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:59.160
Sam does, however, have to transcribe a bunch
of old books – which are almost certainly

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:05.210
gonna contain some kind of important secret
about white walkers or Valyrian steel or Azor

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:06.210
Ahai.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:08.720
Something to help in the war for the dawn.

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:12.790
Meanwhile, however, there’s another war
at hand.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.800
Dany has learned that Euron Greyjoy took out
Yara and the Sand Snakes.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:20.240
So she wants to hunt down Euron’s fleet
on dragonback.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:24.130
This is one of the big advantages of having
dragons – you can scout with them, find

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:26.040
out where enemy armies are.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:29.870
Dany’s ancestor Aegon the Conqueror did
this a lot when he took Westeros.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:34.130
But Missandei’s concerned that an arrow
could kill Dany from dragonback.

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:38.029
You’d think that with some good armour she’d
be pretty safe – and the benefits of scouting

00:12:38.029 --> 00:12:41.610
would be huge – but Dany is convinced, and
stays put.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:46.870
Meanwhile, Grey Worm’s Unsullied attack
Casterly Rock, the seat of Lannister power.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:51.529
This is the first time we’ve seen the Rock
in the show, and it is smaller than the book

00:12:51.529 --> 00:12:55.170
version – it’s built into a rock over
half a kilometre tall.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:13:00.050
Full of tunnels and chambers and mines, the
Rock is the best-defended castle in Westeros

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:05.180
, and the only one that can’t be destroyed
with dragonfire – cause soldiers can hide

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.180
within.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:09.370
But fortunately, Tyrion has a plan.

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:13.690
As in the books, Tyrion worked on the sewers
and drains of the castle, and in the show,

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:17.080
he built a secret tunnel so he could bring
women inside.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:21.440
The Unsullied use this tunnel to get their
forces into the castle – kind of like how

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:23.130
Dany took Meereen.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:27.680
Tyrion says that while Lannisters fight out
of fear, the Unsullied fight “for freedom”,

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:32.710
“And that is why they will triumph” . Which
sounds nice, but is it true?

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:35.970
The Unsullied were raised as children to be
slave soldiers.

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:41.589
They were castrated, psychologically broken,
made “absolutely obedient” . Daenerys

00:13:41.589 --> 00:13:45.080
did “free” them, but do they know what
that means?

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:49.330
If they were truly free, would they choose
to fight and die for this foreign queen in

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:50.480
this foreign land?

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:56.270
It’s nice rhetoric on Tyrion’s part – but
the Unsullied may still be slaves if not in

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:57.360
name.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:01.490
Anyway the Unsullied take Casterly Rock, but
Jaime pulled a switcheroo – most of the

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:03.080
Lannisters weren’t at the Rock.

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:06.670
Jaime led his main army into the reach.

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:11.170
In Season 1, Robb Stark sent a small northern
army to distract Tywin Lannister while his

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:14.000
main force snuck up and captured Jaime.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:18.970
Now in Season 7, Jaime’s strategy is similar,
leaving a small Lannister army at the Rock

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:23.410
to get mulched while his main force attacks
Dany’s allies in the reach.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:27.420
Euron’s ironborn sink Dany’s fleet so
they can’t follow.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.870
This is exactly the sort of thing Dany coulda
seen coming if she used dragons to scout.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:37.180
Or if she used spies under Varys the Spider
. Or if she got Mel to foresee the future.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:41.710
One way or another, Dany really should have
detected the Lannisters marching south, and

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:45.810
the ironborn semi-circumnavigating the continent
again.

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:51.550
But she gets caught by surprise, again, and
the Tyrells have no help against the Lannisters.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:55.350
They would have the support of the Tarlys,
if they didn’t change sides for Cersei.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:58.709
And they might have had the support of the
Redwynes and Hightowers and other reachmen

00:14:58.709 --> 00:15:00.670
– but they’re not seen here.

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:03.120
Maybe they changed sides too, or something?

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:09.120
Whatever the details, the point is that Jaime
takes Highgarden, the seat of Olenna Tyrell.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:13.940
Olenna points out that Jaime carries Widow’s
Wail, Joffrey’s old sword, which happens

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:15.950
to be Valyrian steel.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:20.170
Valyrian steel can kill white walkers – might
come in handy.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:22.950
But mostly Olenna reflects on her life.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:24.310
She’s had a long one.

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:28.340
She’s seen seven kings and now one queen
on the Iron Throne.

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:31.100
She was once betrothed to a Targaryen prince.

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:34.190
And under her guidance, House Tyrell grew
strong.

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:39.330
She says she did terrible things for her family
– but that Cersei beat her in the end because

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:43.770
she did even worse things – murdering Olenna’s
whole family with wildfire.

00:15:43.770 --> 00:15:44.770
Such is the game of thrones.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:49.980
Olenna tells Jaime that Cersei is monstrous,
a disease – and Jaime tries to rationalise

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:51.589
away her evil.

00:15:51.589 --> 00:15:55.560
Olenna observes that Jaime loves Cersei, and
pities him for it.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:16:00.420
She says Cersei will be the end of Jaime – which
does support the valonquar theory, that Cersei

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:03.890
and Jaime will die together – go watch that
video.

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:09.330
Anyway Jaime has Olenna drink poison – a
dignified death, and an appropriate one.

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:13.709
Cause Olenna reveals that she was behind the
poisoning of Joffrey.

00:16:13.709 --> 00:16:19.660
So even at the very end, the Queen of Thorns
sinks one last barb into Cersei – she lets

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:23.070
her know that she killed her cunt of a son.

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:26.880
Olenna dies as she lived, inflicting sick
burns.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:31.870
So this was a huge episode – the death of
the Sand Sneks, the return of Bran, the curing

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:36.880
of Jorah, the fall of the Rock, the death
of Olenna, and the meeting of ice and fire.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:41.690
[A] If you’re curious about these details
from the books – like Jon Connington, and

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:46.130
Cersei and Jaime’s breakup, and the book
versions of Bloodraven and Ellaria and Euron

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:49.320
– you’ve got to go check out the Game
of Thrones books.

